{
  "layer": "solution",
  "type": "component",
  "name": "template-registry",
  "body": "Template registry: hold the merged library's loaded templates (kind by directory: slides/ or sections/), parse each `template.yaml` field schema including an `enum` field's value set (inline `variants:` or a `variants_from:` glob expanded against the layer's `media/` tree — declaring both, or a glob matching nothing, is rejected at load, enum-variants-from) and an `image` field's `roots`/`dir`/`extensions` path options (image-field-roots), run the load-time checks (cycles — a reference is a declared `sections:` acceptance, a `section` helper call in a layout, or a `child` constructor's target, section-helper-load-checks, child-constructor; a declared-section cycle bounded by a declaration's `max_depth` is accepted and walked bounded, bounded-self-nesting —, directory-kind checks, cross-kind name uniqueness, reserved names including `raw`/`data`, a `max_depth` that is not a positive integer, references — including theme CSS references: relative theme `url()`/`@import`, the reserved `media:` prefix resolving under the layer's `media/`, and the reserved `theme:<name>/` prefix resolving under another theme, theme-media-references — and examples), enforce that no name is carried by both library layers (library-layer-uniqueness), resolve a local template's `section` helper call against the merged template set (library-layer-references), execute each template's example layout against the merged layout namespace built from every library layout text keyed by its layer-relative layout name, with the template's own layer function map, so `{{ template \"<name>\" . }}` composition resolves per layer while `media` binds to the template's own layer (example-layout-composition), own the central layout function set (exactly six helpers: `media`, `section`, `dict`, `list`, `child`, `children` — template-language, section-helper, dict-list-helpers, child-constructor, children-forwarding), look up templates, describe them for CLI/gallery.",
